From 51f2ce7de28406079a5aa7a37acf982f4b629216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leozhang <zwj8727@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:10:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] k27: piano-sleep=1: macOS's system sleep as suspend-to-idle
 (CPUs parked in PSCI states, wake sources polled)

The stock arm64 sleep cannot run on this platform: ArmCpu's haltCPU spins in WFI on the calling CPU, its initCPU(false)
panics, this board's arm64_prepare_for_sleep is a WFI loop, and Gunyah's SYSTEM_SUSPEND needs every other vCPU in CPU_OFF,
which ArmCpu cannot undo. So, as Linux's s2idle on this tablet: IOPMrootDomain takes the drivers down as usual, then
IOCPUSleepKernel (piano branch) runs the platform actions and piano_s2idle_enter():

- parks the other CPUs (a bound kernel thread each: preemption and interrupts off, the virtual timer masked, the sleep
  state's PSCI vote via k27 0061's chooser), freezes them with a handshake IPI after which they take no interrupt (so
  nothing runs or stamps a time), and loops on the boot CPU in the deepest state allowed (piano-sleep-state, default ret;
  ss3 only with the LLCC island reserved), its virtual timer the poll clock (piano-sleep-poll, 100 ms), reading the wake
  sources between polls without any driver code: the power key and volume-down (PON INT_RT_STS, SPMI observer), the cover
  opening (TLMM gpio80), the keyboard's status line (gpio95, latched by its owner), a USB-C attach change (Type-C block),
  piano-sleep-max seconds, or a peripheral SPI (piano-sleep-wake selects; default the power key);
- on wake: waits for the power key's release (PianoInput sees no press), moves mach_absolute_time() back by the time
  asleep (no sleep in absolute time, as on a Mac) and has clock_wakeup_calendar() add it to the calendar, releases and
  resyncs the parked CPUs; IOPMrootDomain then wakes the drivers and makes it a full wake (requestUserActive, wake reason
  "piano.<source>" claimed); an aborted suspend (a CPU that does not park) returns at once.
- The Gunyah watchdog is armed from entry, pinged by the loop every 5 s and for 240 s after wake (IOPMrootDomain's 180 s
  wake watchdog panics into it), so a hang resets the tablet (piano-sleep-wdt=0 off; piano-reset-after keeps it).
- piano-sleep=1 overrides the ADT's /defaults sleep-disabled (1 in every native image) at boot completion; without it
  nothing changes. piano-sleep-test=S[,piano-sleep-test-count=N]: kIOPMSleepNow S s after boot and after each wake, with
  piano-sleep-max 30 unless given (unattended tests). machdep.piano_sleep: counts, last duration and reason, RPMh line.
- RPMh sleep counters logged at entry and wake: whether CX and DDR got anywhere (they need the drivers' votes gone: the
  contract in UniXNU-piano package/include/PianoPowerContract.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
